# Data encryption (key made of console buttons)
vault.title = Data encryption
vault.ask.title = Protect your data?
vault.ask.body = To operate, VitaGram stores your data locally on the console: the Telegram session, database, photos, videos, stickers, voice messages and settings. The app can encrypt this local storage to protect it against unauthorized copying.\n\nChoose a console button sequence or a passphrase to unlock it. A passphrase is recommended for better protection.\n\n⚠ If you forget the key, local data cannot be recovered. You will need to delete it and sign in to Telegram again.\n\nYou can manage encryption later in Start > Settings.\n\nPeriodically check in settings that all local files are encrypted. Closing the app or turning off the console during writing may interrupt encryption. Some files may remain unencrypted until the next processing pass or check.\n\nVitaGram does not collect telemetry or send your data to third-party services.\n\nDespite our efforts to improve VitaGram security, the application runs on a modified console with the associated risks. Software with system access may access data in the running application and console memory. Local storage encryption cannot guarantee protection against such access.
vault.ask.footer = {cross} Encrypt data    {circle} Not now
vault.setup.title = Create a key
vault.new.title = New key
vault.setup.hint = Press at least {0} buttons: the D-pad directions, {cross} {circle} {triangle} {square}. Use many different buttons and no simple pattern. Press Start when done.
vault.setup.confirm_title = Repeat the key
vault.setup.confirm_hint = Enter the same sequence again to make sure you remember it.
vault.current.title = Current key
vault.current.hint = Enter your current key and press Start.
vault.disable.title = Turn off encryption
vault.unlock.title = Enter your key
