# About VitaGram
about.title = About

vault.ask.scroll = {dpad}: scroll
about.brand = VitaGram — Telegram for PS Vita
about.version = Version {0}
about.description = An unofficial open-source Telegram client built with VitaSDK, vita2d and TDLib. Chat, read channels and view media on your PS Vita using console buttons and the touchscreen.
about.development = The project is actively developed. Not all Telegram features are available yet, and some features may have limitations or errors.
about.privacy_title = Privacy
about.privacy_servers = VitaGram does not send your messages, files or diagnostic logs to the project author's servers.
about.privacy_logs = Diagnostic logs contain technical information about the application and are disabled by default. VitaGram does not record message text, phone numbers or passwords in them. Logs remain on the console and are never sent automatically. If a problem occurs, you may choose to send logs to the developer manually for troubleshooting.
about.privacy_connections = The client connects to Telegram servers. Update checks and downloads use GitHub. TDLib may also contact external services to resolve proxy hostnames and obtain connection configuration. When a proxy is enabled, the connection passes through your chosen server.
about.security_title = Security and risks
about.security_intro = VitaGram is an unofficial client. Application errors and platform limitations may affect security.
about.risk_data_title = Local storage
about.risk_data = The client stores user data locally on the console. The app can encrypt this storage to protect it against unauthorized copying. Without data encryption, anyone or any software with memory-card access may access local account data and downloaded media.
about.risk_encryption_title = Encryption
about.risk_encryption = Protects local data, but cannot guarantee protection against access to the running application or console memory. Use a long text passphrase: short button sequences are easier to guess. If you lose the key, the encrypted vault cannot be recovered.
about.risk_temporary_title = Temporary files and logs
about.risk_temporary = Some data may briefly remain unencrypted during downloading and processing. Diagnostic logs and separately exported files are not protected by vault encryption. Special diagnostic builds may record folder paths and filenames in the file-picker log.
about.risk_proxy_title = Proxies
about.risk_proxy = Use servers you trust. Their operators may see your IP address and connection metadata. SOCKS5 and HTTP proxies transmit proxy credentials without encryption, while Telegram data remains MTProto-encrypted.
about.risk_updates_title = Installation and updates
about.risk_updates = Install the application from a trusted source. The built-in updater verifies the VPK digital signature before installation.
about.author_title = Author and source code
about.license_title = License
about.license_mit = VitaGram's own code is licensed under MIT. You may use, modify and distribute it, including commercially, provided you retain the copyright notice and license text.
about.license_warranty = The application is provided as is, without warranties. Third-party libraries and fonts have their own licenses.
about.project_link = GitHub · ing156/VitaGram
about.author_link = Telegram · @Ing156
about.footer = {dpad}: scroll  {l}/{r}: page  ←/→: links  {cross}: open  {circle}: back
about.telegram_unavailable = Sign in to Telegram to open the author’s chat.
about.platform_risk = Despite our efforts to improve VitaGram security, the application runs on a modified console with the associated risks. Software with system access may access data in the running application and console memory. Local storage encryption cannot guarantee protection against such access.

